{"Conflicting behavior in SQL expression gating: one finding says SQL expressions remain allowed when the feature flag is enabled via the build path, while another says the reader-side helper rejects QueryTypeSQL unconditionally even when the flag is enabled": 0.8027280569076538, "DuckDB-backed SQL implementation was replaced with pkg/expr/sql.NewInMemoryDB() whose methods are stubs that return 'not implemented', breaking SQL table discovery/validation and execution for SQL expressions": 0.9531176090240479, "SQL expressions documentation still describes the feature as available and instructs users to enable it via the sqlExpressions feature toggle, but the patch blocks SQL expression parsing in code, making these instructions stale and misleading": 0.579250693321228, "Changelog entries describe SQL Expressions as a feature and list the CVE fix but do not reflect that the feature is now disabled in code, leaving the impression that the feature remains available behind a toggle": 0.3968392610549927}